# Predicting Airline Satisfaction

Playground Series - Season 6 Episode 10

**Evaluation metric:** Roc Auc Score
**Data** (read-only, in `/data`):
- `sample_submission.csv`: 299844 rows; columns: id, satisfaction
- `test.csv`: 299844 rows; columns: id, Age, Flight Distance, Inflight wifi service, Departure/Arrival time convenient, Ease of Online booking, Gate location, Food and drink, Online boarding, Seat comfort, Inflight entertainment, On-board service, Leg room service, Baggage handling, Checkin service, Cleanliness, Departure Delay in Minutes, Arrival Delay in Minutes, Gender, Customer Type, Type of Travel, Class
- `train.csv`: 699635 rows; columns: id, Age, Flight Distance, Inflight wifi service, Departure/Arrival time convenient, Ease of Online booking, Gate location, Food and drink, Online boarding, Seat comfort, Inflight entertainment, On-board service, Leg room service, Baggage handling, Checkin service, Cleanliness, Departure Delay in Minutes, Arrival Delay in Minutes, Gender, Customer Type, Type of Travel, Class, satisfaction

**Deliverable:** write `/work/submission.csv` in exactly the format of `/data/sample_submission.csv` (same ids, same
columns). Only the file present at the end counts.

**Rules of this run**
- Time limit: 60 minutes of wall clock; the run is stopped at the limit. Budget your experiments.
- There is no internet access. Python packages already installed are all you have (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn,
  lightgbm, xgboost, catboost, scipy, optuna). Library documentation: `python -c "help(...)"`.
- One research tool is available: the `arxiv` MCP tool (search and read papers submitted before 2026-10-01).
- Work in `/work`. CPU only (4 cores, 16 GB RAM).
